        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0307" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg251"/>

                <head>No. 143.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 9, 1876</date>.
                        (Received June 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 104.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward to you herewith
                    copies of the only notes of any importance which have passed between Lord Derby
                    and myself upon the Winslow matter since my last dispatch upon this subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>





